# NRI tile art

When the user asks to draw / generate / finish map tiles or district sprites:

1. Read **`specs/005-nri-district-map/editor-wishes.md` first** (taste + editor UX + map↔art contracts + **how to draw**: GenerateImage / MCP / knockout).
2. Also follow project skill `.cursor/skills/nri-tile-art/SKILL.md` when generating tiles.
3. Follow `specs/006-nri-tile-art/plan.md` for file drop-in details.
4. Target look: **orthogonal top on the map** (rotates 90° with cell); **¾ isometric iso** only in the cell inspect popup. Not 3/4 on the grid.
5. Still **modular**: sidewalk/canyon around buildings; **roads stay procedural** (no lane paint in building PNG). Cool palette only — no warm tones; housing reads as panel massif; neon from below.
6. Build prompts from wishes §8 + `specs/006-nri-tile-art/prompts.md` (wishes win on conflicts).
7. Final assets → `public/map-tiles/` + `shared/nri-map-art/*-gallery.json` only if they pass the modularity checklist in the wishes doc.
8. Never commit `tmp/` or `dev.db`. Wip drafts stay under `tmp/art-wip/`.
